    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d951">

                <pb facs="0814" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg806"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611b.9417/267</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Chief of the Division of
                        Far Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ballantine</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-02">November 2, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The attached statement appearing on a Japanese Embassy letterhead<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d951-f1"/> was handed to Mr. Ballantine by Mr. Suma of the Japanese
                    Embassy and relates to new measures to make more effective the control of
                    transshipment of Japanese cotton piece goods to the Philippines by way of Hong
                    Kong. Mr. Suma referred to the conversation<anchor n="15" xml:id="d951-f2"/>
                    which Mr. Ballantine had on October 22 with Mr. Sakamoto, First Secretary of the
                    Japanese Embassy, in regard to measures of control previously put into effect,
                    and asked whether there had been any decrease in transshipments. Mr. Ballantine
                    said that the October figures had come in, which showed no decrease over those
                    of the previous month, but he assumed that as the measures referred to by Mr.
                    Sakamoto did not go into effect until October 26, the effect would not be
                    apparent until we receive the November figures.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d951-f3"
                    /></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d951-f1" n="14" xml:id="d951-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d951-f2" n="15" xml:id="d951-f2-content">
                <p>Memorandum of conversation not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d951-f3" n="16" xml:id="d951-f3-content">
                <p>The Japanese Consul General at Manila, Uchiyama, also discussed this problem in a
                    letter of November 5 to the U. S. High Commissioner, McNutt (not printed).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
